# SFT execution status v0.118

2026-09-26. The private controller → guardian → broker/worker doubled-fork
composition is implemented and locally verified with synthetic boundaries.
**The process topology and cleanup wiring are now present, but the fixed role
runtimes and controller event loop are still closed; Gate 5 remains
incomplete.** No real process, socket, descriptor, pidfd, signal, waitid,
cgroup, listener, payload, remote mutation, GPU operation, inference or
training occurred.

## Completed

- Admission requires the frozen Linux/root contracts, one main thread, exact
  cgroup limits/name and parent descriptor, one workload deadline and a bounded
  cleanup suffix before consuming the one attempt.
- Controller precreates the topology, forks guardian, immediately pidfd-binds
  it, closes the controller's cgroup-parent copy and transitions to its exact
  final endpoints plus the guardian pidfd.
- Guardian adopts the inherited topology, reaches `guardian_prefork`, verifies
  the inherited parent descriptor and creates the one cgroup lease before
  nested forks.
- Guardian forks and pidfd-binds broker before forking worker. The later worker
  explicitly identity-checks and closes its inherited broker-pidfd copy before
  transitioning or entering the cgroup.
- Broker and worker adopt their copies, retain only their final topology
  endpoints, close their cgroup-parent copy, join the lease through its leaf FD
  and close that leaf copy.
- Guardian reaches `guardian_watch` only after the parent/leaf descriptors and
  both distinct child pidfds are proven non-aliased. It can create exactly one
  independent CLOEXEC broker-pidfd duplicate for the later fixed watcher.
- Controller, guardian and role wrappers transfer endpoints only through the
  v0.117 one-shot authority adapter. They expose aggregate state without PIDs,
  FDs, descriptor identities or exception text.
- Partial failures continue every independently safe cleanup: lease kill,
  pidfd termination, `waitid(P_PIDFD)` reap, owner close, lease removal,
  inherited-parent close and topology close. Uncertain cleanup remains
  terminal and is never retried.
- Broker, worker and guardian role runtimes remain fixed closed stubs. A
  premature private invocation exits failure after cleanup and cannot execute
  a payload or accept a caller callback.

## Verification

**924 unique tests pass on CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**, with no failures,
errors or skips: 28 new process-composition tests plus the previous 896
regressions. Every new fork, exit, pidfd, cgroup, descriptor, topology, clock,
role and close boundary is synthetic.

Syntax/AST checks pass for both new files on both runtimes; maximum line length
is 88 and trailing whitespace is zero. Tests used `-B`, and no bytecode file
for the new component is present. The five predecessor-plan bindings and all
eight new-plan bindings match their recorded sizes and SHA-256 values.

